+| `SettingsBackdropConfiguration` | SettingsUIStyle | Host-owned backdrop values and preset conversion |
+| `SettingsGlassOpacityCurve` | SettingsUIAuthoring | Validated opacity mapping for the background effects controls |
+| `SettingsGlassSurface`, `SettingsGlassReflectiveSurface` | SettingsUIStyle | Native glass below opaque foreground content, with optional decorative artwork |
+| `SettingsGlassConfiguration`, `SettingsGlassRecipe`, `SettingsGlassCapabilities` | SettingsUIStyle | Validated glass settings, authored defaults, and effective renderer capabilities |
+| `SettingsGlassWindow`, `SettingsGlassPanel` | SettingsUIStyle | Host-owned native windows with configurable active appearance |
+| `SXYControl` | SettingsUI | Two-axis input with a custom visual field, live readouts, help, and keyboard actions |
+| `SInventoryRow` | SettingsUI | Selection and hover treatment for inventories |
+| `SettingsCategoryBar` | SettingsUI | Horizontal category choices with a menu fallback |
+| `SettingsWorkspace` | SettingsUI | Stable inventory and detail identity across column and drawer layouts |
+| `SettingsColumnResizeHandle` | SettingsUI | Bounded pointer, keyboard, and accessibility width adjustment |
+| `SettingsBackdrop` | SettingsUIStyle | Decorative animation with window focus, visibility, and Reduce Motion gating |
+| `SShortcutBadge`, `SShortcutHint`, `SShortcutAction` | SettingsUI | Consistent shortcut display and action hover hints |
+| `SKeyboardShortcutRow` | SettingsUIKeyboardShortcuts | Optional KeyboardShortcuts-backed editor for one or multiple shortcuts |
+
+`SShortcutBadge` defaults to a compact pill. Use `.keycaps` for individual key
+tokens or `.plain` for bold symbols without a pill. `SShortcutHint` pairs a
+label with one or more badges. Attach `.settingsShortcutHover(_:shortcuts:)` to
+any view for the default hover hint, or use `SShortcutAction` to get a button
+with that hint built in. The explicit `.settingsShortcutPopover(isPresented:...)`
+modifier supports click-triggered details.
+
+For editable settings, add the `SettingsUIKeyboardShortcuts` product and pass
+a binding to `SKeyboardShortcutRow`. It accepts either a single optional
+`KeyboardShortcuts.Shortcut` or an array for multiple assignments. The adapter
+exposes `.settingsShortcut` for display, so the same host-owned value can drive
+the settings editor and action hint. The host registers actions and persists
+shortcuts through its own KeyboardShortcuts setup.
+
+Click a shortcut to record a replacement; the field shows modifiers as they are
+held and saves as soon as a valid shortcut is pressed. Escape cancels, Tab or a
+click elsewhere leaves, and Delete removes the shortcut being edited. Pass
+`allowsRemoval: false` for a required shortcut; Delete then explains that a
+shortcut is needed and keeps recording. Keys need ⌘, ⌥, or ⌃ unless they are
+function keys. Shortcuts already used by macOS, by a menu item, by another
+assignment in the row, or rejected by the host's `validateShortcut` are refused
+in place with a reason below the row. The app's registered KeyboardShortcuts
+are paused while any row records.
 
 `SettingsCategoryBar` receives your category models and selection binding. The
 host normalizes selection when its available categories change.
 
+`SSectionCard` can omit its heading and divider with `showsHeader: false` and
+`showsDivider: false`. This keeps compact pages from repeating a heading already
+shown by their parent view.
+
+The new controls are demonstrated on the example's Components page. Their
+bindings remain host-owned. `SDetentSlider` accepts any finite stops in its
+range; capture and release distances are points along the native slider track.
+Use `presentation: .compact` for inspector columns that already show a value.
+It keeps the native track continuous and puts concise, clickable stop values
+below it. Use two or three short labels; accessibility uses the full formatter.
+
+```swift
